55
00:05:43,528 --> 00:05:50,088
First of all, if you have a constant, derivation of constant numbers, constant functions are zero.

56
00:05:50,468 --> 00:05:54,747
So if you have a constant, the derivation of the constant will be zero.

57
00:05:56,208 --> 00:06:00,768
If you have two functions and if you have a plus or minus between these two functions,

58
00:06:00,927 --> 00:06:06,048
and if you want to take derivation of these functions, you will take the first function's derivation.

59
00:06:06,048 --> 00:06:14,427
If it is plus, it will be plus. If it is minus, it will be minus, plus or minus the second function's derivation.

60
00:06:14,528 --> 00:06:18,627
I think you know these two rules.

61
00:06:19,348 --> 00:06:24,687
If you have a multiplication with a constant, you can write this constant outside of the derivation.

62
00:06:25,307 --> 00:06:27,807
It will be c product du over dx.

63
00:06:28,187 --> 00:06:30,987
Mostly we will use these two rules.

64
00:06:30,987 --> 00:06:38,108
If you have a product of two functions, and if you want to take derivation of these two functions,

65
00:06:38,687 --> 00:06:42,708
it will be the first function's derivation product the second function,

66
00:06:43,127 --> 00:06:47,848
plus the first function product the second function's derivation.

67
00:06:48,648 --> 00:06:51,067
This is the rule for product.

68
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:59,187
And if you have a division, the u over v, it will be the first function's derivation product the second function,

69
00:06:59,567 --> 00:07:07,268
minus the first function product the second function's derivation over square of the denominator.

70
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:08,228
Okay.

71
00:07:09,268 --> 00:07:12,687
This is the main rules about derivation, not function.

72
00:07:12,687 --> 00:07:19,108
